{
 "meta": {"level": "A2", "section": "Verbs", "number": 9, "total_in_level": 10,
  "title": "The imperative and polite requests",
  "subtitle": "Kom binnen, laten we gaan, zou je ... kunnen, and the softeners even, maar and eens",
  "footer": "Language Learning · A2 · Verbs · The imperative and polite requests",
  "next": "Next: A2 · pdf 10 — Vocabulary and phrases"},
 "blocks": [
  {"type": "callout", "kind": "tip", "title": "After this PDF you can", "bullets": [
   "give instructions with the <b>imperative</b>: <i>Kom binnen. Ga zitten.</i>",
   "make suggestions with <b>laten we</b>",
   "ask politely with <b>Kun je ...?, Zou je ... kunnen?, Wilt u ...?</b>",
   "soften a request with <b>even, maar</b> and <b>eens</b>"]},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "1. The imperative"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "The imperative is simply the <b>stem</b> of the verb: <i>werken → <b>Werk</b>!, komen → <b>Kom</b> binnen!, gaan → <b>Ga</b> zitten.</i> It is the same for one person or more. Separable prefixes go to the end: <i><b>Bel</b> me morgen <b>op</b>.</i> The only irregular one: <b>zijn → wees</b> (<i>Wees voorzichtig</i>, be careful)."},
  {"type": "table", "style": "plain", "widths": [4.2, 6.6, 6.2], "head": ["Infinitive", "Imperative", "English"], "rows": [
   ["komen", "Kom binnen.", "Come in."],
   ["gaan zitten", "Ga zitten.", "Sit down."],
   ["opletten", "Let op!", "Watch out! Pay attention!"],
   ["zijn", "Wees stil.", "Be quiet."],
   ["vergeten", "Vergeet je sleutels niet.", "Don't forget your keys."],
   ["niet roken (sign)", "Niet roken.", "No smoking."]]},
  {"type": "callout", "kind": "note", "title": "No 'don't' in Dutch", "text": "English needs <i>don't</i> for a negative imperative. Dutch just adds <b>niet</b> or <b>geen</b>: <i>Rook <b>niet</b>. Maak je <b>geen</b> zorgen.</i> On signs and in instructions Dutch often uses the infinitive: <i>Niet roken. Hier parkeren verboden. Duwen.</i> (Push.)"},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "2. Suggestions: laten we"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "For <i>let's</i>, Dutch says <b>laten we</b> + infinitive at the end: <i><b>Laten we</b> naar huis <b>gaan</b>. <b>Laten we</b> morgen <b>afspreken</b>.</i> In speech <b>Zullen we ...?</b> is just as common: <i>Zullen we gaan?</i>"},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "3. Polite requests"},
  {"type": "table", "style": "plain", "widths": [7.2, 5.6, 4.2], "head": ["Dutch", "English", "Tone"], "rows": [
   ["Kun je het raam even dichtdoen?", "Can you close the window?", "normal, friendly"],
   ["Zou je me kunnen helpen?", "Could you help me?", "polite"],
   ["Wilt u hier even tekenen?", "Would you sign here, please?", "polite, formal"],
   ["Mag ik de rekening?", "Can I have the bill?", "normal"],
   ["Zou u langzamer kunnen praten?", "Could you speak more slowly?", "very polite"],
   ["Komt u binnen.", "Do come in.", "formal imperative with u"]]},
  {"type": "callout", "kind": "tip", "title": "Dutch sounds direct, and that's fine", "text": "A Dutch imperative is less rude than an English one: <i>Geef me het zout even</i> is normal at the table. But to strangers, in shops and at work, a question with <b>kun je, zou je</b> or <b>wilt u</b> is safer. <b>alsjeblieft</b> / <b>alstublieft</b> at the end makes it polite."},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "4. The softeners: even, maar, eens"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Small words make an imperative friendlier. They have no direct English translation; they change the tone, not the meaning (more in B2 · pdf 3)."},
  {"type": "table", "style": "plain", "widths": [2.6, 6.6, 7.8], "head": ["Word", "Effect", "Example"], "rows": [
   ["even", "just, quickly: a small favour", "Kun je even helpen? Wacht even."],
   ["maar", "go ahead, no problem: permission", "Kom maar binnen. Ga maar zitten."],
   ["eens", "try this: a suggestion", "Kijk eens. Probeer het eens."],
   ["toch", "come on: urging", "Kom toch mee!"]]},
  {"type": "verbpairs", "title": "Useful phrases", "items": [
   ["Wacht even.", "Wait a moment."], ["Kom maar binnen.", "Do come in."], ["Ga maar zitten.", "Have a seat."],
   ["Kijk eens.", "Have a look."], ["Let op!", "Watch out!"], ["Pas op!", "Be careful!"],
   ["Maak je geen zorgen.", "Don't worry."], ["Doe maar rustig.", "Take it easy."], ["Laten we gaan.", "Let's go."],
   ["Ga je gang.", "Go ahead."]]},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "5. Common mistakes"},
  {"type": "mistakes", "rows": [
   ["Komt binnen!", "Kom binnen!", "Imperative: the stem."],
   ["Ben voorzichtig.", "Wees voorzichtig.", "zijn: wees."],
   ["Doe niet roken.", "Rook niet.", "No do: just niet."],
   ["Laat ons gaan.", "Laten we gaan.", "Let's: laten we."],
   ["Opbel me morgen.", "Bel me morgen op.", "Separable: prefix at the end."],
   ["Zou je kunnen me helpen?", "Zou je me kunnen helpen?", "The infinitives go to the end."],
   ["Maak je niet zorgen.", "Maak je geen zorgen.", "Before a noun: geen."]]},
  {"type": "h1", "text": "6. Self-check"},
  {"type": "p", "text": "Fill in the missing word. The answers are on the last page."},
  {"type": "exercises", "items": [
   {"q": "______ binnen!", "hint": "komen", "a": "kom", "full": "Kom binnen!"},
   {"q": "______ voorzichtig op de fiets.", "hint": "zijn", "a": "wees", "full": "Wees voorzichtig op de fiets."},
   {"q": "Bel me morgen ______.", "hint": "opbellen", "a": "op", "full": "Bel me morgen op."},
   {"q": "______ we naar huis gaan.", "hint": "let's", "a": "laten", "full": "Laten we naar huis gaan."},
   {"q": "______ je me kunnen helpen?", "hint": "could", "a": "zou", "full": "Zou je me kunnen helpen?"},
   {"q": "Wacht ______. Ik kom eraan.", "hint": "a moment", "a": "even", "full": "Wacht even. Ik kom eraan."},
   {"q": "Ga ______ zitten. Wil je koffie?", "hint": "permission, friendly", "a": "maar", "full": "Ga maar zitten. Wil je koffie?"},
   {"q": "Kijk ______ wat ik heb gekocht!", "hint": "suggestion", "a": "eens", "full": "Kijk eens wat ik heb gekocht!"},
   {"q": "Maak je ______ zorgen.", "hint": "no worries", "a": "geen", "full": "Maak je geen zorgen."},
   {"q": "______ u hier even tekenen?", "hint": "polite, would you", "a": "wilt", "full": "Wilt u hier even tekenen?"},
   {"q": "Vergeet je jas ______.", "hint": "don't forget", "a": "niet", "full": "Vergeet je jas niet."},
   {"q": "Pas ______! Een fiets!", "hint": "be careful", "a": "op", "full": "Pas op! Een fiets!"}]},
  {"type": "p", "text": "<b>Translate into Dutch:</b>"},
  {"type": "translations", "items": [
   {"q": "Come in.", "a": "Kom binnen."},
   {"q": "Don't worry.", "a": "Maak je geen zorgen."},
   {"q": "Could you help me?", "a": "Zou je me kunnen helpen?"},
   {"q": "Let's go home.", "a": "Laten we naar huis gaan."}]},
  {"type": "pagebreak"},
  {"type": "answers"}
 ]
}
